{#- Consumer adapter for packs/castle-changelog-release-pack
    templates/CHANGELOG.md.tmpl (marketplace v0.1.0).

    Why this file exists (failed edge, ledgered in docs/sjira/v26.9.21/C7.md):
    the pack's template speaks ggen's frontmatter dialect (to: + named
    sparql: queries), but ggen 26.8.18's declarative [[generation.rules]]
    pipeline — the schema this repo's consumer bootstrap landed on — renders
    rule templates as plain Tera with the rule query bound to `results`, and
    does not parse template frontmatter ("frontmatter template lint are not
    implemented for the declarative-rules schema yet", ggen-engine). Pack
    resolution ([[packs]] -> TemplateSource::Pack) is likewise typed against
    the other schema only.

    Adaptation is therefore minimal and mechanical: the two set lines below
    bind the pack template's named result sets (`releases`, `entries`) from
    the rule's UNION query, and the ENTIRE body that follows is the pack
    template verbatim (header, closed six-category grouping, [YANKED] and
    Unreleased handling). The marketplace is the owning source; when ggen
    implements pack resolution or frontmatter parsing for declarative rules,
    delete this adapter and point template.file back at the pack template.
    Consumers must not edit the body below; edit schema/changelog.ttl facts
    and re-run `ggen sync run`. -#}
{%- set releases = results | filter(attribute="version") -%}
{%- set entries = results | filter(attribute="description") -%}
{% raw %}# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

{% endraw %}
{%- set categories = ["Added", "Changed", "Deprecated", "Removed", "Fixed", "Security"] -%}
{% for release in releases %}
{%- if release.version == "Unreleased" -%}
## [Unreleased]
{%- else -%}
## [{{ release.version }}]{% if release.date %} - {{ release.date }}{% endif %}{% if release.yanked %} [YANKED]{% endif %}
{%- endif %}
{% set release_entries = entries | filter(attribute="rel", value=release.rel) %}
{%- for cat in categories %}
{%- set cat_entries = release_entries | filter(attribute="category", value=cat) %}
{%- if cat_entries | length > 0 %}

### {{ cat }}

{% for entry in cat_entries %}- {{ entry.description }}
{% endfor -%}
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{% endfor -%}
